From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: allow unused imports in cli tunnel and update-service sources

The reh-archive and architecture CLI patches rewrite the `use` statements in `code_server.rs`, `dev_tunnels.rs`, and `update_service.rs`, leaving some imports unused; the crate-level `#![allow(unused_imports)]` suppresses the resulting Rust warnings so the CLI still compiles cleanly.

diff --git a/cli/src/tunnels/code_server.rs b/cli/src/tunnels/code_server.rs
index a3df1bea0edfb12ffdec847044bea885868d7c2b..15c123d3d6d03c921f65e66b35d5511bf47db9f5 100644
--- a/cli/src/tunnels/code_server.rs
+++ b/cli/src/tunnels/code_server.rs
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
  *  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.
  *  Licensed under the MIT License. See License.txt in the project root for license information.
  *--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
+#![allow(unused_imports)]
+
 use super::paths::{InstalledServer, ServerPaths};
 use crate::async_pipe::get_socket_name;
 use crate::constants::{
